    "updated_at": "2026-09-14T07:29:02Z",
    "body": "I used https://everythingfonts.com/subsetter and https://cloudconvert.com/ttf-to-woff2, subsetting the bold font to:\r\n\r\n```\r\nCSaegilnst\r\n```\r\n(SteelCastings)\r\n\r\nand the non-bold to:\r\n\r\n```\r\n*,-./0123456789:;ABCGHMPSTUYabcdefghiklmnoprstuvx\r\n```\r\n(All other characters in the table)\r\n\r\n`unicode-range` is not needed since the font is definitely needed; there's no font fallback for any glyph in the table.\r\n\r\nIt looks the same in Firefox, Safari, Chrome. Tested by running `./build.sh` and editing `output/index.html` to reference the local `styles.css` and using this `styles.css` and the new font files. Screenshots with Firefox:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1600\" height=\"404\" alt=\"Screenshot with subsetted font.\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bdcc2c19-b961-4d18-8090-8a5e006cc072\" />\r\n<img width=\"1600\" height=\"404\" alt=\"Screenshot reference.\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/adc9de06-60ac-4cd9-a341-648299fa0bb9\" />",
